          "function": "cavity_geometry",
          "feature": "sampled_grid_clearance_statistics_A__mean",
          "physical_role": "Mean clearance over a dense grid; higher (or less negative) mean values reflect overall lattice openness and availability of interstitial space."
        },
        {
          "function": "cavity_geometry",
          "feature": "sampled_grid_clearance_statistics_A__std",
          "physical_role": "Standard deviation of sampled clearances; captures heterogeneity of void sizes, distinguishing structures with isolated large cages from those with uniformly small pores."
        },
        {
          "function": "structure_summary",
          "feature": "metal_site_fraction",
          "physical_role": "Fraction of metallic (including transition\u2011metal) sites; provides the conductive backbone that can stabilise delocalised interstitial electrons, as observed in transition\u2011metal silicide electrides."
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "The seven descriptors map directly onto the four physical pillars identified in the literature: (i) electropositive chemistry (alkali_alkaline_site_fraction, pauling_electronegativity__min), (ii) electronegativity contrast (pauling_electronegativity__std), (iii) cavity size and accessibility (max_clearance_A, sampled_grid_clearance_statistics_A__mean, sampled_grid_clearance_statistics_A__std), and (iv) a metallic framework (metal_site_fraction). Each feature is scalar, non\u2011redundant (except the intentional inclusion of both mean and std clearances to capture complementary aspects of void geometry), and available in the catalog, providing an interpretable basis for a gradient\u2011boosting classifier.\n    ",
